# Overview
#
# `respectively`, `the former`, and `the latter` make the reader map
# each item back to an earlier list (`The two flags set the host and the
# port respectively`), and the mapping breaks when someone reorders the
# list. The fix repeats the noun, or it pairs each item with its value
# in one clause (`The host flag sets the host, and the port flag sets
# the port`). A clause is a subject and its verb, such as `the tests
# pass`. The rule sits at Recommended, because `former` and `latter` are
# also plain adjectives, and the rule skips only the nouns in its list.
#
# Expression
#
# `sense` lists the nouns that the adjectives `former` and `latter`
# take, and the filter skips `the former` and `the latter` before one of
# them. Harper's part-of-speech tagger marks a verb after `the former`
# as a noun (`The former drops writes`), so a part-of-speech guard
# cannot replace the list. A negated word after a space needs a word to
# consume, so the branch has a twin for the end of a clause. The twin
# takes `the latter.` and `the former,`.
#
# False Positives
#
# `former` and `latter` are also plain adjectives (`the former
# maintainer`, `the latter half`), so the phrase passes before a noun in
# `sense`.
#
# Measurement
#
# The rule hit 69 lines in the measure.py corpus, and 19 of 20 sampled
# hits pointed back at an earlier list. The one misfire was the plain
# adjective before a noun outside `sense` (`the former User-Agent`).
expr sense [
    maintainer,
    maintainers,
    owner,
    owners,
    employee,
    employees,
    member,
    members,
    colleague,
    colleagues,
    partner,
    partners,
    president,
    head,
    half,
    part,
    parts,
    stage,
    stages,
    years,
    days,
    decades
]
expr main [respectively, <(the [former, latter] !@sense), (the [former, latter])>, (the [former, latter][., ;, :, (,)])]
let message "`former`, `latter`, or `respectively`. Repeat the noun, or pair each item with its value."
let description "Flags `respectively`, `the former`, and `the latter`, which make the reader map items back to an earlier list."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
let scope "Sentence"
allows "The former maintainer wrote the parser."
allows "The latter half of the file is empty."
allows "The host flag sets the host, and the port flag sets the port."
